-- title:
--   Base change of the Y-chart of a projective Weierstrass model
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $R$, and $K$ a commutative ring equipped with an $R$-algebra structure. Inside the statement, $\psi$ denotes the graded ring homomorphism from $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,3)\,R$ modulo the ideal generated by the homogeneous Weierstrass cubic of `W.toProjective`, graded by the images of the homogeneous submodules, to the corresponding quotient for the base-changed curve `W.map (algebraMap R K)`: it is the map induced on quotients by coefficientwise application of $R \to K$ to polynomials, well defined because the image of the span of the cubic of $W$ is the span of the cubic of the base-changed curve, and graded because coefficient extension preserves homogeneity of each degree. The assertion is that the following square of affine schemes is a pullback: the map $\mathrm{Spec}$ of `Away.map ψ` at the class of the variable `X 1` (the chart $D_+(Y)$), from the $Y$-chart of the base-changed model to the $Y$-chart of $W$; the structure morphism of the base-changed $Y$-chart to $\mathrm{Spec}\,K$, given by $K$ mapping into the degree-zero component followed by the canonical map into the away-localisation; the analogous structure morphism of the $Y$-chart of $W$ to $\mathrm{Spec}\,R$; and $\mathrm{Spec}$ of $R \to K$.
--
--   This records that forming the standard affine chart $D_+(Y)$ of the projective Weierstrass model commutes with base change, i.e. the $Y$-chart ring of the base-changed model is $K \otimes_R$ the $Y$-chart ring of $W$, expressed schematically as a pullback square. It is one of the three chart cases assembled in [`WeierstrassProjModel.kw_bc_awayIsPushoutAll`](thm.html#WeierstrassProjModel.kw_bc_awayIsPushoutAll), which supplies base-change compatibility for the projective model used in the study of models of elliptic curves.
-- source:
